        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0313" n="205" xml:id="pg205"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States,<lb/>Costa Rica, Nicaragua, and
                                Salvador</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1893-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July 27, 1893</hi></date>. (Received September 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor of submitting to you the
                    inclosed brief correspondence between Hon. A. H. Rivas, who occupied the
                    position of minister of foreign relations under the Zavala administration, and
                    myself in reference to the removal of the American legation to Granada for
                    safety on a recent occasion.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker.</hi></signed></closer>



